{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782436237,"nonce":"Ix0ctHLmOAcUv9qj8oD2qAvElBU=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGwjA9g","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/333","origin":"github"},"title":"Speed → throttle (PWM) characterization + 2026-06-25 power analysis","message":"## Summary\n\nAdd a **speed → throttle (PWM)** characterization to the power reference, and commit the\n**2026-06-25 deployment power analysis** (`docs/analysis/2026-06-25/`).\n\nMined from this week's four Massabesic lake surveys (2026-06-22/23/24/25) via the\n`bag_analysis` SQLite pipeline. Two complementary views:\n\n- **Steady straight-line** (achieved odom speed, |yaw|\u003c0.05 rad/s) — the clean\n  hydrodynamic speed→throttle relationship.\n- **Ramp-inclusive** (actual `rc/out.ch_0` binned by **commanded**\n  `setpoint_velocity/cmd_vel.vel_x`, no steady filter) — approximates typical survey-ops\n  duty, capturing accel-onto-line and post-turn recovery.\n\n## Key findings\n\n- Throttle %% = `(PWM−1500)/5`. Sustaining the survey band: ~2.75 kt ≈ 57 %%, **3.0 kt ≈ 64 %%,\n  3.2 kt ≈ 70 %%, 3.5 kt ≈ 81 %%**. The PWM→speed map is strongly super-linear.\n- **Ramp overhead at a given commanded speed is small (+0–4 pts)** — the controller tracks\n  well; re-acceleration episodes are brief relative to time-on-line.\n- The genuinely new finding from the commanded-speed view: a **current-heavy post-turn\n  recovery regime** (~7 %% of survey time at cmd ~3.9 kt / ~94 %% throttle / ~61 A, but the\n  hull only reaches ~3.1 kt) — a tuning lever (gentler post-turn ramp trades line-acquisition\n  time for lower peak current).\n- **Cost knee ~3.0–3.1 kt:** current rises gently below it, then steeply (~34 → ~47 A from\n  3.1 → 3.5 kt). ~3.0 kt (a touch over) is the practical cruise sweet spot — just past the\n  ~2.9 kt range-optimal, before the steep cost ramp.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- `docs/analysis/2026-06-25/README.md` + plots (dock-departure voltage, speed-vs-curve,\n  commanded-speed → throttle/current).\n- `bizzyboat_project11/docs/bizzyboat_power.md` — speed↔throttle table + sweet-spot/knee framing.\n\nPart of the power-characterization thread. Partially fills the throttle dimension of\n#88 (opportunistic field data, not the controlled bench PWM×current sweep #88 still calls for).\nFollows deployment #331.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}